    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82814" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεττεία</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετρ-ευτής</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετρ-εύω</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετρ-ός</span></b> , 
			Att.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεσσεία</span>, etc. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεττύκια</span></b> , τά, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>clippings of
				leather</i>, Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.305
			</span></i> P. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεσσύγγιον</span>.) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέττω</span></b> , 
				Att.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέσσω</span>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πευδρία:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτοθήκη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πευθείς</span></b>  (i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεφθείς</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
			ἑψηθείς</span>, Id. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεύθη</span></b> , ἡ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
				ʽπεύθομαἰ</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεῦσις</span>
			, Id.</div>
